{{#is_alert}}More than 5% of MotherDuck queries failed in the last 15 minutes.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}More than 2% of MotherDuck queries failed in the last 15 minutes.{{/is_warning}}

Check the *Errors* group on the MotherDuck dashboard for the error types and the users affected, then `SELECT error_type, error_message, user_name, query_text FROM md_information_schema.query_history WHERE error_type IS NOT NULL ORDER BY start_time DESC LIMIT 50`.

@slack-data-platform

p95 query latency on MotherDuck has been above {{threshold}} ms for 15 minutes (now {{value}} ms).

Look at *Slowest query per minute by instance type* and *Top users by slowest query* on the MotherDuck dashboard; a single Mega/Giga duckling saturated by one user is the usual cause.

@slack-data-platform

A MotherDuck query has been running for more than {{threshold}} seconds.

Find it with `SELECT user_name, start_time, query_text FROM md_information_schema.recent_queries` (rows with a NULL end_time are still running).

@slack-data-platform

Queries on {{instance_type.name}} ducklings spilled more than 100 GB to disk in the last 30 minutes. Spilling means the working set no longer fits in memory: consider a larger instance size, narrower projections, or splitting the job.

See *Top users by bytes spilled to disk* on the MotherDuck dashboard.

@slack-data-platform

MotherDuck Flight **{{flight_name.name}}** had a failed run in the last 30 minutes.

Read its logs in the MotherDuck UI (Flights > {{flight_name.name}}) or with `MD_GET_FLIGHT_LOGS`.

@slack-data-platform

Active storage across the MotherDuck organization grew {{value}}% over the last day.

See *Largest databases* and *Active bytes per database* on the MotherDuck dashboard to find the database responsible.

@slack-data-platform

No heartbeat from the MotherDuck Datadog exporter Flight for 15 minutes, so every other MotherDuck monitor is blind.

Check the `datadog-exporter` Flight in MotherDuck: is its schedule active, did the last run fail, is the Datadog API key still valid?

@slack-data-platform

The MotherDuck exporter's **{{collector.name}}** collector has failed on every run for 15 minutes; the metrics it produces are stale.

`storage_info` failing usually means the Flight's token is not an organization admin. Otherwise read the Flight run logs for the warning line.

@slack-data-platform
